WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:00.960
What's the therapy?

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:03.600
Could you show us how to do it?

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:04.080
Okay?

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.560
Let’s show you a move from Yiguan

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:13.947
The Yiguan move works the upper back, then down to just above the waist

00:00:14.003 --> 00:00:16.720
We place one on each side

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:22.116
Five at each point, one on each side—twelve in all

00:00:22.164 --> 00:00:27.516
As you move your right side over, move your butt the other way

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:31.478
Your upper and lower body should move apart

00:00:31.527 --> 00:00:35.760
Move your butt over, then flow through the motion

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:38.824
Not about you

00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:42.928
Beginners often do it wrong and end up

00:00:43.648 --> 00:00:45.145
Swaying side to side

00:00:45.186 --> 00:00:46.148
That’s wrong

00:00:46.208 --> 00:00:46.848
Why?

00:00:46.848 --> 00:00:50.629
Your spine curves in an S. When your upper body moves this way

00:00:50.663 --> 00:00:55.248
move the other way; when your lower body moves this way, move the other
way

00:00:55.248 --> 00:00:57.408
So cross your movements like this

00:00:57.568 --> 00:01:02.848
With an S-shaped curve, you can do it this way; your body will adjust on its
own

00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:03.968
Just twist like this

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.320
Twisting is quite interesting

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:16.084
To care for your spine, you can do this at home—no cupping needed

00:01:16.131 --> 00:01:18.400
Just sway from side to side

00:01:19.952 --> 00:01:23.232
As you sway, you can move your elbows up and down

00:01:23.392 --> 00:01:25.712
This position targets this vertebra

00:01:25.872 --> 00:01:29.552
Raise your elbows a little to target this area of the spine

00:01:29.712 --> 00:01:33.412
You can sway like this, and this side too

00:01:34.752 --> 00:01:38.752
A simple, comfortable move that’s great for your spine

00:01:38.752 --> 00:01:42.352
Next, Dr. Wu, please show us the inchworm exercise

00:01:42.752 --> 00:01:46.212
Let’s demonstrate the inchworm exercise

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:50.832
For the inchworm, straighten your arms, then twist your body like this

00:01:50.912 --> 00:01:56.112
Okay, I’ll demonstrate the twist now so everyone can see it more clearly

00:01:56.112 --> 00:01:58.112
Next, lie down and twist like this

00:01:58.272 --> 00:02:02.352
As you twist, move your hips up and down

00:02:02.512 --> 00:02:06.164
Keep both arms straight

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:11.952
Then start by pressing both feet down

00:02:11.952 --> 00:02:16.272
Move your hips up and down like this

00:02:16.912 --> 00:02:20.032
Twist your spine from side to side

00:02:20.752 --> 00:02:22.772
Sway 20 times

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:29.424
Then, when you’re done, lift both feet up... and sway again

00:02:30.224 --> 00:02:35.921
You’ll notice the stretch and muscle sensation when your feet are

00:02:35.972 --> 00:02:40.704
flexed feels different from when you press them down

00:02:40.704 --> 00:02:47.104
This gives the whole spine......a full-body adjustment

00:02:47.184 --> 00:02:52.304
If you don’t have scoliosis, this is a great way to maintain your spine

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:57.504
Finally, how do you do the side-to-side hip sway with your hands on your
hips?

00:02:57.584 --> 00:03:01.184
Let’s go over the hands-on-hips hip sway

00:03:01.184 --> 00:03:09.984
The key is to rest your calves on a raised cushion, about 20 to 30
centimeters high

00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:16.464
Put your hands on your hips, around the top of your hip bones

00:03:16.464 --> 00:03:21.824
Then sway your hips from side to side

00:03:22.064 --> 00:03:25.534
After swaying side to side 10 times

00:03:25.591 --> 00:03:31.604
move your hands up about two finger-widths and sway again

00:03:31.584 --> 00:03:39.504
Do three rounds, alternating between the middle, upper, and lower
positions

00:03:39.584 --> 00:03:41.818
I’ll demonstrate lying down

00:03:41.865 --> 00:03:45.984
Put your hands on your hips and lift your buttocks

00:03:46.064 --> 00:03:50.000
Then sway your hips from side to side

00:03:51.344 --> 00:03:53.829
Use your waist, where your hands rest, as the pivot

00:03:53.857 --> 00:03:54.864
Move back and forth

00:03:55.104 --> 00:04:02.704
When arching your back, relax a little and rest your buttocks on the bed,
then continue

00:04:02.704 --> 00:04:08.804
After the cross, move both hands up to this spot, where your fingertips are

00:04:09.584 --> 00:04:11.924
Then rock side to side in the middle

00:04:13.104 --> 00:04:14.724
Then rock side to side below

00:04:15.824 --> 00:04:17.124
Then rock side to side above

00:04:17.504 --> 00:04:20.903
The iliac crest sits around the waist

00:04:20.958 --> 00:04:27.744
near the lumbar vertebrae that are prone to problems—roughly L2 to L5

00:04:27.904 --> 00:04:33.664
Rocking side to side helps loosen the muscles and ligaments on either
side of the spine

00:04:33.984 --> 00:04:37.245
Once loosened, the stuck joint surfaces can open up

00:04:37.281 --> 00:04:39.984
and the bones can gradually return to place

00:04:40.144 --> 00:04:48.506
But there’s something important to watch for: if this movement makes your
back pain

00:04:48.563 --> 00:04:55.664
numbness, or tingling worse, it may not be right for you, so stop for now

00:04:55.664 --> 00:05:00.224
After rocking for a while, your spine can gradually realign from side to side

00:05:00.259 --> 00:05:01.184
It’s that simple

00:05:01.344 --> 00:05:03.424
Thank you, Dr. Wu, for that wonderful demonstration

00:05:03.664 --> 00:05:11.250
To prevent scoliosis from worsening, what should patients pay attention to
in daily life

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.487
when lying down, sitting, or resting?

00:05:14.538 --> 00:05:17.684
Could you share some tips, Dr. Wu?

00:05:18.464 --> 00:05:20.536
First, maintain good posture

00:05:20.578 --> 00:05:21.288
Actually

00:05:21.288 --> 00:05:27.148
Scoliosis isn’t always caused by poor posture

00:05:27.308 --> 00:05:27.468
Mm

00:05:27.628 --> 00:05:32.028
It’s strange—it can progress very quickly during puberty

00:05:32.028 --> 00:05:40.748
Even without poor posture, good posture can help prevent scoliosis from
worsening

00:05:40.748 --> 00:05:43.308
So that’s something to keep in mind

00:05:43.308 --> 00:05:47.035
Also, don’t stay in one position for a long time

00:05:47.082 --> 00:05:54.128
Even with good posture, people with scoliosis can get uncomfortable if
they sit too long

00:05:54.108 --> 00:05:56.985
Since their posture is already affected

00:05:57.029 --> 00:06:03.148
they should get up and move around or stretch regularly if they sit for a
long time

00:06:03.148 --> 00:06:06.201
Also, watch your sleep position; try not to sleep on your stomach

00:06:06.201 --> 00:06:09.751
Sleeping on your stomach puts pressure on your neck

00:06:09.751 --> 00:06:18.286
Your chest may also cave downward, which can cause problems and affect
your spine

00:06:18.286 --> 00:06:21.408
Also, avoid carrying heavy loads

00:06:21.408 --> 00:06:25.868
Carrying heavy things puts strain on your body, so be careful

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:30.682
You may need to avoid certain activities, like long-distance running

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:34.228
ballet, rhythmic gymnastics, and even swimming

00:06:34.228 --> 00:06:40.188
But isn’t swimming symmetrical and therefore helpful for spinal balance?

00:06:40.188 --> 00:06:48.788
Although swimming is symmetrical, with strokes like freestyle and
breaststroke

00:06:48.851 --> 00:06:57.635
people with scoliosis......may use one side more because their strength is
uneven

00:06:57.697 --> 00:07:07.388
This can create muscle imbalances and may actually worsen their
scoliosis, so be careful

00:07:07.388 --> 00:07:11.268
Lastly, change your diet and make sure you get enough nutrients

00:07:11.268 --> 00:07:18.155
Studies show that people who are underweight are more likely to have low
bone density

00:07:18.201 --> 00:07:20.903
which is associated with scoliosis

00:07:20.948 --> 00:07:28.062
Among women with scoliosis, 27 to 38 percent have low bone density
throughout the body

00:07:28.108 --> 00:07:34.068
For those with more severe curves, that figure may be as high as 47
percent

00:07:34.068 --> 00:07:39.040
Dr. Wu, your advice on scoliosis today has been fascinating and very
practical

00:07:39.077 --> 00:07:41.268
Could you briefly sum it up for us?

00:07:42.592 --> 00:07:43.072
Sure

00:07:43.232 --> 00:07:46.112
Scoliosis can be quite difficult to treat

00:07:46.192 --> 00:07:52.947
As we mentioned, if your curve is severe, see a specialist who treats
scoliosis

00:07:52.998 --> 00:07:57.892
The goal is to treat it without surgery whenever possible

00:07:58.032 --> 00:08:01.792
If these three methods we discussed help you
